# check: fail error[E8a, E4a]: this shift is past its literal's width, and nothing adapts it to a wider type
# E4a/E8a: "1 << 64" adapted to a wider type would be computed exactly; with nothing adapting it, it is an I64 shift by
# 64, its literal's own type's (T6a), which E8a leaves undefined - so it is an error, as a written amount past a typed
# value's width is
fn main() ? {
    t := $(1 << 64)
}
